<!--
  Recovery-free drive tree for the narrow-entrance recovery.

  Same replanning pipeline as nav_to_pose_short_recovery.xml - 1 Hz
  ComputePathToPose, then FollowPath - with every recovery action removed:
  no ClearEntireCostmap, no BackUp, no Spin, no RetryNode around the planner
  or the controller.

  Why (2026-11-21, red_cube_1 -> C): the recovery must be the only thing that
  decides whether to retreat, wait or give up. With the stock trees each failed
  attempt was followed by Nav2's own 0.5 m back-up and 0.8 rad spin and a
  double costmap clear, so the base left the staging point on its own, the
  recovery's "came back to the same pose" assumption broke, and the log read
  like the recovery had cleared the maps (it had not - the behaviour tree had).

  A failure here therefore means exactly one thing: from the current start cell
  the planner or the controller refused, with the base still where the recovery
  put it, and the recovery's own classification is the only authority.
-->
<root main_tree_to_execute="MainTree">
  <BehaviorTree ID="MainTree">
    <PipelineSequence name="NavigateWithoutRecovery">
      <RateController hz="1.0">
        <ComputePathToPose goal="{goal}" path="{path}" planner_id="GridBased"/>
      </RateController>
      <FollowPath path="{path}" controller_id="FollowPath"/>
    </PipelineSequence>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
